# No Major Glitches rules:

1. Notable examples of **allowed** skips/techniques are:

    - Interacting through a wall;

    - Skipping/speeding up objectives via in-bounds parkour (e.g. grabbing the goat from the outside of the burning building on Goat Simulator day 1) or by completing certain objectives earlier than intended (e.g. getting the keycard early on Golden Grin Casino);

    - Exploiting the quirks in the game mechanics, such as Golden Grin Casino lasers skip (said lasers having a slight periodic activation delay, allowing you to pass through without triggering them, if timed correctly.), despawning guards on White House and other edge cases like that are allowed;

    - Mask-up slowmotion.

    - As well as update-specific mechanics like:

        - Mask up animation cancelling (update 240.2);

        - Old escape methods (e.g. Mallcrasher van escape on update 23);

        - Old objective mechanics/timers (e.g. Ukrainian Job escape timer pre-update 175);

        - Old game mechanics (e.g. old assault mechanics on pre-update 181);

        - Snowballs (update 232.X and 240+ in steam offline mode);

        - Pre-changes perkdecks (e.g. Copycat switch speed pre-update 236).

2. Major glitches are **NOT allowed**, that includes:

    - PBSH (the spamming pause to "fly" glitch);

    - Collision Removal (removing collisions of animated objects, such as doors with projectiles);

    - Sniper Collision (update 233-specific bug with the Aran G2 sniper, that allows you to spawn a small rectangular collision whenever you swap to said sniper);

    - Going OOB (out of bounds);

    - Warping (the "teleport" glitch);

    - Bag duplication;

    - Animation Desync (spamming pause to desync objects to gain some kind of advantage: i.e. the truck on Goat Simulator d1 to secure every goat instantly);

    - Update-specific developer mistakes that allow for unintended and highly significant timesaves (i.e. Aftershock’s missing heli timer script on update 93 or bypassing the burning of the money on Firestarter d3 by securing a loot bag on update 22.1 or below).

For more detailed information on technique restrictions for each category, see “The Speedrunning Guide”. (Coming Soon)

